IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `hra-dates`

-- Health Records Act 2001 (Vic) -- the rules the questions share: the answers' enumerations, the s 3 definitions more
-- than one question uses (health information, immediate family member), and the three duties with deadlines run as
-- regulative rules (s 34(2) answer to an access request; s 34(2)(b)(ii) access after the fee is paid; HPP 6.9 decision
-- on a correction request), with the helper that runs each over what happened.
--
-- The questions are asked in hra-seat.l4, which IMPORTs this module; where a provision is used by one question only, the
-- seat module applies its words there and cites them. Nothing here is exported.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no rule answers JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no ("means", "if, and only if",
-- "must not", "nothing in this Act applies", "does not", "need not", "unless", "if" conditions that fail, a period the
-- text fixes); or NOTHING where the Act does not answer on the facts given, with a "NOTHING-kind" comment. Judgments
-- the Act hands to the organisation, the Health Complaints Commissioner or the Tribunal ("believes on reasonable
-- grounds", "considers", "satisfied", "reasonably necessary", "sufficient interest", "in accordance with guidelines")
-- are inputs: the answer is conditional on them, never a guess.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Health Records
-- Act 2001, Version No. 050 (1 May 2026), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published with the
-- authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in accordance with the
-- Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Health Records Act 2001`

§§ `s 3 -- definitions`

-- s 3(1) "health information means -- (a) information or an opinion about -- (i) the physical, mental or psychological
-- health (at any time) of an individual; or (ii) a disability (at any time) of an individual; or (iii) an individual's
-- expressed wishes about the future provision of health services to him or her; or (iv) a health service provided, or
-- to be provided, to an individual -- that is also personal information; or (b) other personal information collected to
-- provide, or in providing, a health service; or (c) other personal information about an individual collected in
-- connection with the donation, or intended donation, by the individual of his or her body parts, organs or body
-- substances; or (d) other personal information that is genetic information about an individual in a form which is or
-- could be predictive of the health (at any time) of the individual or of any of his or her descendants -- but does not
-- include health information ... that is prescribed as exempt health information".
-- "personal information means information or an opinion ... whether true or not, and whether recorded in a material
-- form or not, about an individual whose identity is apparent, or can reasonably be ascertained, from the information or
-- opinion, but does not include information about an individual who has been dead for more than 30 years". Both are
-- "means" definitions: TRUE or FALSE.
GIVEN `it is about my health, a disability, my wishes about future health services, or a health service to me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was collected to provide, or in providing, a health service`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was collected in connection with my donation of body parts, organs or substances`                    IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is genetic information that could predict my or my descendants' health`                              IS A BOOLEAN
      `my identity is apparent or can reasonably be ascertained from it`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have been dead for more than 30 years`                                                                IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is prescribed as exempt health information`                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 -- it is health information` `it is about my health, a disability, my wishes about future health services, or a health service to me` `it was collected to provide, or in providing, a health service` `it was collected in connection with my donation of body parts, organs or substances` `it is genetic information that could predict my or my descendants' health` `my identity is apparent or can reasonably be ascertained from it` `I have been dead for more than 30 years` `it is prescribed as exempt health information` IF
        `it is personal information`
    AND (    `it is about my health, a disability, my wishes about future health services, or a health service to me`
          OR `it was collected to provide, or in providing, a health service`
          OR `it was collected in connection with my donation of body parts, organs or substances`
          OR `it is genetic information that could predict my or my descendants' health`)
    AND (NOT `it is prescribed as exempt health information`)
    WHERE
        `it is personal information` MEANS `my identity is apparent or can reasonably be ascertained from it` AND (NOT `I have been dead for more than 30 years`)

-- s 3(1) "immediate family member of an individual means a person who is -- (a) a parent, child or sibling of the
-- individual; or (b) a spouse or domestic partner of the individual; or (c) a member of the individual's household who is
-- a relative of the individual; or (d) a person nominated to a health service provider by the individual as a person to
-- whom health information relating to the individual may be disclosed". "relative of an individual means a grandparent,
-- grandchild, uncle, aunt, nephew or niece"; "sibling ... includes a half-brother, half-sister, adoptive brother,
-- adoptive sister, step-brother or step-sister"; "parent, in relation to a child, includes" a step-parent, adoptive or
-- foster parent, guardian, or a person with custody or daily care and control of the child.
DECLARE `Relationship to me` IS ONE OF
    `my parent`
    `my child`
    `my sibling`
    `my spouse or domestic partner`
    `a relative living in my household`
    `a relative not living in my household`
    `a person I nominated to the health service provider`
    `someone else`

GIVEN `the relationship` IS A `Relationship to me`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 -- an immediate family member` `the relationship` IF
    CONSIDER `the relationship`
    WHEN `my parent` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `my child` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `my sibling` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `my spouse or domestic partner` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a relative living in my household` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a person I nominated to the health service provider` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `Duties with deadlines`

DECLARE `What became of the duty` IS ONE OF
    `done in time`
    `not done in time`
    `still open`

DECLARE `Organisation` IS ONE OF
    `the organisation`

DECLARE `Organisation's act` IS ONE OF
    `answer my access request`
    `give me access after the fee is paid`
    `notify me of its decision on my correction request`

-- s 34(2): "Within 45 days after receiving a request, the organisation must -- (a) give to the individual a written
-- reason for refusal of access ...; or (b) if the organisation is charging a fee ... -- (i) give to the individual a
-- written notice stating that the organisation will give access ... on payment of the fee ...; and (ii) give access ...
-- within 7 days after payment of the fee or 45 days after receiving the request, whichever is the later; or (c) in
-- every other case, give access ... as soon as practicable but not later than 45 days after receiving the request."
-- The first duty: one of the three answers (written refusal, fee notice, or access) within 45 days. Failing it, the
-- organisation "is taken to have refused access" (s 35(a)). Days counted from receipt.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Organisation` `Organisation's act`
`s 34(2) -- the organisation must answer my access request` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the organisation`
    MUST `answer my access request`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the organisation` BECAUSE "the organisation did not, within 45 days after receiving the request, give a written reason for refusal, a written notice of the fee, or access; it is taken to have refused access (s 34(2), s 35(a))"

-- s 34(2)(b)(ii): access "within 7 days after payment of the fee or 45 days after receiving the request, whichever is
-- the later". Days counted from receipt of the request to that later day.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Organisation` `Organisation's act`
`s 34(2)(b)(ii) -- the organisation must give me access after the fee is paid` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the organisation`
    MUST `give me access after the fee is paid`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the organisation` BECAUSE "the organisation did not give access within 7 days after payment of the fee or 45 days after receiving the request, whichever is later; it is taken to have refused access (s 34(2)(b)(ii), s 35(a))"

-- HPP 6.9: "If an individual requests an organisation to correct health information about the individual, the
-- organisation must take reasonable steps to notify the individual of a decision on the request as soon as practicable
-- but in any case not later than 30 days after the request is received by the organisation." Days from receipt.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Organisation` `Organisation's act`
`HPP 6.9 -- the organisation must notify me of its correction decision` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the organisation`
    MUST `notify me of its decision on my correction request`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the organisation` BECAUSE "the organisation did not notify the decision on the correction request within 30 days after receiving it (HPP 6.9); this may be an interference with privacy (s 18) open to complaint (s 45)"

-- The helper that runs a duty over what happened (in the shape of the Coroners Act 2008 encoding's helper). On the
-- stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH: where the act was done, FULFILLED means in
-- time and anything else late; where it was not, the helper asks whether doing it now would still be in time. It takes
-- a DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
GIVEN `the rule`                    IS A DEONTIC `Organisation` `Organisation's act`
      `the act`                     IS AN `Organisation's act`
      `the act has been done`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time the act was done`   IS A NUMBER
      `the time now`                IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`what became of the organisation's duty` `the rule` `the act` `the act has been done` `the time the act was done` `the time now` MEANS
    IF `the act has been done`
    THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time the act was done`), (EVENT `the organisation` `the act` `the time the act was done`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `done in time`
         OTHERWISE `not done in time`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time now`), (EVENT `the organisation` `the act` `the time now`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `still open`
         OTHERWISE `not done in time`

-- s 34(2) by dates: the last day is the 45th day after the day the request was received.
GIVEN `the day the request was received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 34(2) -- the last day to answer` `the day the request was received` MEANS `the date` 45 `days after` `the day the request was received`

-- s 34(2)(b)(ii) by dates: the later of 7 days after payment and 45 days after receipt.
GIVEN `the day the request was received` IS A DATE, `the day the fee was paid` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 34(2)(b)(ii) -- the last day to give access` `the day the request was received` `the day the fee was paid` MEANS
    `the later of` (`the date` 7 `days after` `the day the fee was paid`) `and` (`the date` 45 `days after` `the day the request was received`)

-- HPP 6.9 by dates: the last day is the 30th day after receipt.
GIVEN `the day the request was received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`HPP 6.9 -- the last day to notify the decision` `the day the request was received` MEANS `the date` 30 `days after` `the day the request was received`
